1
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:07,580
Man, the look in his eyes is so intense...

2
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:11,380
And that's how he looks after running
for nearly 30 minutes straight?

3
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:14,500
Meanwhile, I've only run 
for like 2 or 3 tops.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,580
Shit!

5
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:17,420
What is it, Chucky?

6
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:19,750
Nothing, forget what I just said!

7
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:20,580
Huh?

8
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:22,880
We don't have to change our 
zone formation, either!

9
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:26,840
All I gotta do is put a 
stop to their #7, right?

10
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:30,840
Until Tinytown is back in the game,

11
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:35,130
I'll shut down #7 even if it means
I have to slug him in the face!

12
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:37,670
Kitasumi!

13
00:00:36,670 --> 00:00:37,670
Full-court?!

14
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:38,670
Let's score!

15
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:39,680
Kitasumi!

16
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:41,100
Can their #6 really run enough to cover him?!

17
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,100
Let's score!

18
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:42,290
Kitasumi!

19
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:44,080
Again? Give me a break.

20
00:00:42,290 --> 00:00:44,080
Let's score!

21
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,830
Tinytown kept it up for a full 30 minutes.

22
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:50,470
Lasting a measly 10 minutes 
should be a piece of cake!

23
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:54,460
Chucky, you brave fool! Men 
like you are one of a kind!

24
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:57,680
Guys... I'm counting on 
you to handle things here!

25
00:00:58,540 --> 00:00:59,590
Huh?

26
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:03,630
He shook him off again!

27
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:03,630
Oh no, Chucky!

28
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:05,720
Your defense is too weak.

29
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,090
Huh?

30
00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:14,800
WHAAAAAAAAT?!

31
00:01:14,830 --> 00:01:17,130
What the hell are you doing?!

32
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:18,970
Come back! Come back! Come back!

33
00:01:18,970 --> 00:01:23,300
Nobody said anything about 
doing triangle and 2!

34
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:50,380
Ahiru no Sora

35
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:55,710
Come back! Come back! Come back!

36
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:59,670
Nobody said anything about 
doing triangle and 2!

37
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:59,670
Now...

38
00:02:59,670 --> 00:03:03,260
If you do that, it'll leave only 
3 of us to defend the middle!

39
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:05,160
Triangle and 2?

40
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:08,180
Two defenders mark a single opposing player, while

41
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:10,670
the rest defend the basket in a zone formation.

42
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:12,040
Just leave them be.

43
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:12,880
Huh?

44
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:15,290
They're both half-assed 
players to begin with.

45
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:18,300
Putting the two of them together
might actually accomplish something.

46
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:20,540
Oh, good point. That makes sense.

47
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:25,090
It doesn't make sense! What the hell are
the 3 of us left behind supposed to do now?!

48
00:03:25,210 --> 00:03:29,580
Their 2 low post players are nearly here!
Chiaki and I will just have to hold firm in the middle!

49
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,720
Kite! Don't stray too far out of the zone!

50
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:36,790
They're really doing everything they can
to shut Taro down.

51
00:03:36,790 --> 00:03:39,130
It's a pretty drastic strategy to rely on.

52
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:43,340
It just ended up like that on 
a whim, but.... it could work.

53
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:46,330
Don't let him get past 
you on that side, Nabe!

54
00:03:46,330 --> 00:03:48,450
We're fine as long as you don't screw it up!

55
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:52,380
Close call!

56
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:55,610
Everyone's counting on me to cover for Tinytown!

57
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:58,300
I'm not letting you past me without a fight!

58
00:03:58,330 --> 00:04:00,090
Chucky...

59
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:02,090
Taro! Pass the ball back!

60
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:10,680
We let him slip right past us!

61
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:12,380
Idiots!

62
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:15,130
That's what happens when you both
take your eyes off the ball!

63
00:04:15,170 --> 00:04:16,340
Huh?

64
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:18,610
Right back at you.

65
00:04:18,610 --> 00:04:19,750
A steal!

66
00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:21,080
Whoa! Nice, Kite!

67
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:24,380
Wh-wh-wh-wh... WHAT?!

68
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:29,130
The pillar that's holding their zone defense together
is definitely that #11.

69
00:04:29,130 --> 00:04:30,040
Huh?

70
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:34,000
Their #8 and #5 both caused a lot of holes
in their defense, but thanks to help from #11

71
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,420
they've been avoiding any major disasters.

72
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:40,460
He's also been the source of 
about 60% of their points.

73
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:42,040
No way! Back off!

74
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:45,080
Give me the ball! I'm gonna score enough
to make their heads spin!

75
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:46,580
I see what he's doing.

76
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:49,430
Since they've lost one of 
their offensive players,

77
00:04:49,630 --> 00:04:53,180
he's trying to keep the defense focused
on himself instead.

78
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:54,680
I'm quite impressed.

79
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:58,010
We're going to have to go 
all-in to put a stop to him.

80
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:03,510
Kite... he's looking really worn out.

81
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:15,790
They're going for a double team, too?!

82
00:05:15,790 --> 00:05:19,300
An eye for an eye. Or something like that.

83
00:05:19,790 --> 00:05:22,510
Are you sure two is gonna be enough, old man?

84
00:05:27,710 --> 00:05:30,800
He slipped right in-between them!
Holy shit! That's awesome!

85
00:05:33,130 --> 00:05:34,330
He got stopped!

86
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:36,220
Our help moved faster than him!

87
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:38,710
He's surrounded!

88
00:05:38,710 --> 00:05:39,860
A triple team?!

89
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:42,130
Bunch of morons!

90
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,750
We got the ball! It's a turnover!

91
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:47,050
Go now! Get moving! Make a fast break!

92
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,220
Kite!

93
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,870
The defense is wide open!

94
00:05:51,870 --> 00:05:54,430
You're not getting by me, dammit!

95
00:06:00,130 --> 00:06:01,300
Konishi!

96
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:06,920
Kuzuryu
Kitasumiyoshi

97
00:06:04,130 --> 00:06:06,920
Whoa! Nice teamwork!

98
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,840
Way to go, Konishi!

99
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,840
Shit!

100
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:13,260
Our team is going to win.

101
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,590
You punk...

102
00:06:15,670 --> 00:06:18,170
Listen up, Momoharu. Kite.

103
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:19,800
We've only got a minute left.

104
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,970
We have to finish this quarter with the lead.

105
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:25,150
It'll keep our momentum
and give us an edge in the last quarter!

106
00:06:25,330 --> 00:06:29,340
Boys! Go and get on 'em quick! 
Push for that comeback!

107
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:40,670
They've switched over to full-court D!

108
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:43,550
Wh-what kind of defense is this?!

109
00:06:43,670 --> 00:06:46,430
The 2-2-1 zone press!

110
00:06:48,330 --> 00:07:02,220
Defense! Defense! Defense! Defense!

111
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:52,580
Get up in their faces!

112
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:57,970
There is a proper time and place
to use a full-court defense, you know.

113
00:07:03,710 --> 00:07:11,010
Kitasumi! Kitasumi! Kitasumi!

114
00:07:04,330 --> 00:07:05,760
Nice cut!

115
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:12,630
The lead is ours!

116
00:07:11,290 --> 00:07:14,240
Kuzuryu
Kitasumiyoshi

117
00:07:12,630 --> 00:07:14,240
Hell yeah! Let's go!

118
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:18,790
Hurry and pass the ball in!
If we don't spread out fast, they'll snatch it again!

119
00:07:18,790 --> 00:07:20,720
Watch out for steals!

120
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:25,000
Sweet! He got past 'em!

121
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,460
No... they set him up!

122
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:31,970
A back tip steal!

123
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:39,470
Kuzuryu
Kitasumiyoshi

124
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:39,430
Awesome! Two baskets in 
a row, just like that!

125
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,580
Yeah! Show them who's boss, Senpai!

126
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:45,680
Kitasumi! Kitasumi! Kitasumi!

127
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:50,090
Well shit, we're screwed
without another decent dribbler on our side.

128
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:52,000
Dammit!

129
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,840
How many times am I gonna let
Konishi get the better of me?!

130
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:58,460
All it took was a damn press 
to make us totally fall apart.

131
00:07:58,460 --> 00:08:00,750
We're still a pretty pathetic team.

132
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:03,750
I haven't even done much, but 
I'm suddenly exhausted...

133
00:08:03,750 --> 00:08:07,260
What is up with this defense?! 
We can't do a damn thing!

134
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:10,670
The momentum totally shifted
to the other team in an instant.

135
00:08:11,210 --> 00:08:12,470
Hey, Nanao...

136
00:08:14,090 --> 00:08:16,460
Everybody work together to 
get the ball down the court!

137
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:18,560
Be careful not to get an 8-second violation!

138
00:08:19,130 --> 00:08:20,300
Hey, Nanao.

139
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:27,050
Uh, what is it? I couldn't hear you.

140
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:29,680
I've rested long enough.

141
00:08:31,250 --> 00:08:33,280
Let's make a substitution.

142
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:39,720
A substitution? But there are only 30 seconds left in the third quarter!

143
00:08:41,830 --> 00:08:44,160
I'm fully aware of that.

144
00:08:45,790 --> 00:08:47,180
But...

145
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:50,470
Kuzuryu
Kitasumiyoshi

146
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:53,130
...I have to get out there.

147
00:08:54,290 --> 00:08:55,800
Right now!

148
00:08:57,630 --> 00:08:58,920
Defense! Defense! Defense!

149
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:00,080
All right.

150
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:05,510
Defense! Defense! Defense!

151
00:09:02,830 --> 00:09:05,510
Out of bounds! Kuzuryu ball!

152
00:09:09,630 --> 00:09:12,590
Player substitution for Kuzuryu High!

153
00:09:15,830 --> 00:09:17,830
Nanano must be an idiot.

154
00:09:17,830 --> 00:09:20,090
We're stressed out enough, adding another

155
00:09:20,090 --> 00:09:22,170
good-for-nothing is only going to make it worse.

156
00:09:22,670 --> 00:09:24,680
Hey, Kite. You're subbing out.

157
00:09:24,790 --> 00:09:25,830
Huh?

158
00:09:25,830 --> 00:09:29,040
"Natsume is giving us a bad rep
by looking like a deadbeat out there."

159
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,340
Nanao's orders.

160
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,790
I never said anything like that!

161
00:09:33,790 --> 00:09:36,260
Wh-what a relief...

162
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:37,630
Oh, hey, Nabe!

163
00:09:37,630 --> 00:09:38,330
Huh?

164
00:09:38,330 --> 00:09:40,880
That was the best triangle 
and 2 I've ever seen!

165
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:42,720
Nice defense!

166
00:09:43,130 --> 00:09:46,340
I see... so my defense is the best ever, huh?

167
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:48,880
Then maybe I'll go back out later!

168
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:52,290
I've had it up to here with these guys,
they're all so self-absorbed!

169
00:09:52,290 --> 00:09:55,090
The training camp changed
absolutely nothing about them!

170
00:09:55,210 --> 00:09:57,790
Listen up! Nobody hold on 
to the ball for too long!

171
00:09:57,790 --> 00:10:00,460
We know. Just set me some screens.

172
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:05,340
Chucky. If they press us again, try not to panic.
Watch your surroundings closely.

173
00:10:07,830 --> 00:10:09,870
I guess they have changed a little.

174
00:10:10,710 --> 00:10:13,790
Considering the height difference,
she should have kept #8 in.

175
00:10:13,790 --> 00:10:16,340
That was a pretty reckless substitution.

176
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:21,130
Kuzuryu
Kitasumiyoshi

177
00:10:16,670 --> 00:10:20,970
Well, only 30 seconds left.
Let's see how many times we can score on them.

178
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:24,170
Okay, they've got him cornered!

179
00:10:24,170 --> 00:10:25,830
#7 can't move very fast!

180
00:10:25,830 --> 00:10:27,260
Let's steal and score again!

181
00:10:27,670 --> 00:10:29,210
Don't stop moving!

182
00:10:29,210 --> 00:10:31,460
Hurry and get into an open pass window!

183
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:32,590
Hey, Chiaki!

184
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:43,450
Ah, this is much better.

185
00:10:43,450 --> 00:10:46,460
I'd rather be on the court
than the bench no matter how tired I am!

186
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:52,790
Although, I do feel bad for rebelling
against Nanano and ignoring her orders...

187
00:11:01,170 --> 00:11:05,380
Everyone else is out here giving their all.
I can't just take it easy!

188
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:06,750
Okay!

189
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:08,090
Don't worry!

190
00:11:08,130 --> 00:11:10,340
We'll definitely catch up with them!

191
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:13,970
Dumbass. Nobody needs you to tell them that.

192
00:11:14,210 --> 00:11:18,720
I don't really know why, but I feel
a lot more confident with him on the court.

193
00:11:19,750 --> 00:11:22,110
Don't show off too much.

194
00:11:22,750 --> 00:11:24,250
He went straight for it!

195
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:25,960
But he's not getting by our guys!

196
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:28,430
Hey! Enjoy your little nap?

197
00:11:29,250 --> 00:11:30,710
He's right at the sideline!

198
00:11:30,710 --> 00:11:31,880
They've got him cornered!

199
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:34,180
Taro! Behind you! It's a screen!

200
00:11:34,750 --> 00:11:36,800
Weak sauce. That won't work on me!

201
00:11:39,670 --> 00:11:41,220
WHAT THE-?!

202
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:44,170
He just straight-up ignored 
my brilliant screen!

203
00:11:44,170 --> 00:11:46,470
Hot damn, he blew past both defenders!

204
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:47,710
Hey ref!

205
00:11:47,710 --> 00:11:50,430
Are you sure he didn't cross 
the line with that move?!

206
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:54,480
Once again, his ability to cut in
proves essential to the team.

207
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:55,710
#4 has it now!

208
00:11:55,710 --> 00:11:56,970
Don't let him get through!

209
00:11:59,540 --> 00:12:01,590
Whoa! Nice return pass!

210
00:12:03,990 --> 00:12:06,920
You're too easy! Such a piece of cake!

211
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:09,540
I bet your granny calls you a "sweet boy"!

212
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:11,870
What's wrong? You look out of breath!

213
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:14,680
Are you sure you shouldn't 
be watching from the bench?!

214
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:17,040
He's not stopping!

215
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:18,460
Is he seriously going for it?!

216
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,750
I'm the best player here!

217
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:23,340
You're nothing but a crazy nutjob!

218
00:12:27,430 --> 00:12:30,340
Goddamn! Could you have made
that pass any harder to catch?!

219
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:34,220
Go ask Chiaki to give you
some passing lessons, dumbass!

220
00:12:35,350 --> 00:12:37,630
Kuzuryu
Kitasumiyoshi

221
00:12:35,710 --> 00:12:37,310
He nailed it!

222
00:12:37,670 --> 00:12:39,830
Give me some cash, I'm 
making sure Kite gets paid.

223
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:41,590
Get your own, dammit!

224
00:12:41,710 --> 00:12:44,250
Crap, they broke through our 
press defense and scored!

225
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:46,510
Now we're only 3 points ahead!

226
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:50,040
There's nothing to panic about.
It won't kill our momentum.

227
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:53,760
We'll score the last basket
and end this quarter with a 5-point lead.

228
00:12:57,460 --> 00:13:00,300
What?! Defending before 
the ball even goes in?!

229
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:01,790
Ready, Chucky?

230
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:03,210
You know it!

231
00:13:03,210 --> 00:13:07,890
There's still a few seconds left on the clock!
Let's get that ball and score another basket!

232
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,880
Those dumbasses!

233
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:12,380
There's hardly any time left 
anyway! Let's back them up!

234
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:13,880
Seriously...?

235
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:20,220
What are you doing?! Hurry 
and pass it out of there!

236
00:13:20,330 --> 00:13:21,630
Only 6 seconds left!

237
00:13:25,250 --> 00:13:26,800
That ball is ours!

238
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:35,510
Over here!

239
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,590
Hey, Chucky!

240
00:13:42,210 --> 00:13:43,080
The pass went through!

241
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:46,430
Chucky! CHUCKY!

242
00:13:48,710 --> 00:13:50,010
Sora...

243
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:52,630
Taro! Don't let him shoot a three!

244
00:13:52,630 --> 00:13:54,210
You don't have to tell me!

245
00:13:54,210 --> 00:13:56,000
This brat is nearly dead on his feet!

246
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,340
There's no way I'm letting 
him score one on us!

247
00:13:58,670 --> 00:13:59,880
I will.

248
00:14:12,420 --> 00:14:14,700
That's the end of the third quarter!

249
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:18,160
Wha-wha-wha-wha-wha-wha-wha-?!

250
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:18,160
Insane...

251
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:20,880
Kuzuryu
Kitasumiyoshi

252
00:14:18,540 --> 00:14:20,880
Th-they tied it up?!

253
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:22,840
Ow, ow...

254
00:14:24,460 --> 00:14:26,210
I'm so glad that went in.

255
00:14:26,210 --> 00:14:27,750
That little punk!

256
00:14:27,750 --> 00:14:30,500
I'm definitely gonna make him pay for this!

257
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,580
Yo, are you all right?

258
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:34,130
Thanks, Chucky.

259
00:14:36,290 --> 00:14:38,170
That was a nice pass!

260
00:14:38,170 --> 00:14:39,350
Thanks!

261
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:42,460
Man, that kid really is something else.

262
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:44,930
I could've tied us just as easily.

263
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:49,880
I told him not to show off!

264
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:53,750
It's the last quarter of the game
and the score is all tied up.

265
00:14:53,750 --> 00:14:57,540
Kuzuryu
Kitasumiyoshi

266
00:14:54,250 --> 00:14:56,880
I bet nobody expected that.

267
00:14:57,540 --> 00:15:00,220
We can win this! We WILL win this!

268
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:02,760
Listen, I want everybody to review what we practiced

269
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:05,120
during training in their heads one last time!

270
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,380
Especially our defensive formations!

271
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:09,500
We need to watch out for #7
coming at us from long-range.

272
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:11,670
He's definitely started to 
find his stride out there.

273
00:15:11,670 --> 00:15:13,130
Right!

274
00:15:13,130 --> 00:15:14,580
No problem.

275
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,580
I won't let him get open 
to take a shot that easily!

276
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:18,830
Y-you can count on me for some points, too!

277
00:15:18,830 --> 00:15:21,680
I promise I'll do everything 
I can not to get ejected!

278
00:15:21,790 --> 00:15:23,710
I'm ready to sub in for anybody!

279
00:15:23,710 --> 00:15:25,830
So go out there and play 
until you're ready to drop!

280
00:15:25,830 --> 00:15:28,130
If we manage to win this game...

281
00:15:29,290 --> 00:15:31,590
...let's all go out for BBQ.

282
00:15:33,990 --> 00:15:36,290
Why does it have to be BBQ?

283
00:15:36,290 --> 00:15:38,080
Because I'm really hungry.

284
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:40,330
Dude, I don't have that kind of money.

285
00:15:40,330 --> 00:15:43,050
Don't sweat it. We've got financial backing.

286
00:15:46,830 --> 00:15:48,080
I like this plan.

287
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,710
Now that you mention it,
my tummy's been grumbling for a while now.

288
00:15:50,710 --> 00:15:53,510
Stop right there! I never 
agreed to pay for anything!

289
00:15:53,670 --> 00:15:57,510
Just so you know, I paid for this training camp
out of my own pocket!

290
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:00,340
Do you boys think teachers 
are made out of money?!

291
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:02,600
Calm down, Mr. Satsuki.

292
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:13,290
BBQ! BBQ! BBQ!

293
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:06,080
Please just go ahead and 
make the promise with them.

294
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:08,420
We'll have our hands full if 
they start causing a riot.

295
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:09,830
Yes, but...

296
00:16:09,830 --> 00:16:13,290
You don't have to worry. 
They can't win anyway.

297
00:16:13,290 --> 00:16:18,290
BBQ! BBQ! BBQ!

298
00:16:18,290 --> 00:16:20,660
Think about it, a team like ours that

299
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:24,010
just got their start stands no chance against a veteran school.

300
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:26,590
Fair enough.

301
00:16:26,830 --> 00:16:28,540
V-very well then!

302
00:16:26,830 --> 00:16:31,330
BBQ! BBQ! BBQ!

303
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:31,330
I'll treat you to BBQ if 
you win. So do your best!

304
00:16:31,330 --> 00:16:33,010
YES!

305
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:36,340
You know, I really like our teach.

306
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:37,880
All right!

307
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,880
We're totally gonna win this thing!

308
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,930
I overheard you, manager.

309
00:16:42,790 --> 00:16:45,590
So, that's what you really think about us?

310
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:47,380
I was lying, obviously.

311
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:49,670
I did it to help spur everyone on.

312
00:16:49,670 --> 00:16:51,830
And also so we can chow down on BBQ!

313
00:16:51,830 --> 00:16:55,050
I've done more than enough of cooking
for all of you guys!

314
00:16:56,250 --> 00:16:57,800
What a schemer...

315
00:16:58,670 --> 00:17:00,090
Something the matter?

316
00:17:01,670 --> 00:17:03,000
What are you talking about?

317
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,830
Well, you seem kinda off your game.

318
00:17:04,830 --> 00:17:07,310
Despite all the rebounds you made
in the Maru high game,

319
00:17:07,310 --> 00:17:08,970
you've barely made any today.

320
00:17:09,170 --> 00:17:11,880
Quit nitpicking. Just leave me alone.

321
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:14,580
Where are you going, Momoharu?

322
00:17:14,580 --> 00:17:16,010
To take a piss.

323
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:25,130
Dammit, Konishi! Are you listening?!

324
00:17:25,130 --> 00:17:27,270
Uh, yessir!

325
00:17:27,270 --> 00:17:30,670
Look, you are going to be
our key player in the last quarter.

326
00:17:30,670 --> 00:17:33,720
As long as they're playing zone D,
then it's a battle between centers.

327
00:17:33,790 --> 00:17:37,760
Stick to the low-post alongside Tachibana.
If you do a good job at...

328
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:44,540
How awesome, Konishi!
Despite being a freshman, everyone's relying on you!

329
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:47,130
Do the rest of us proud out there! Okay?

330
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:53,790
Their center has yet to score any baskets.

331
00:17:53,790 --> 00:17:57,290
From what I can tell it seems like
he's hardly tried to shoot at all.

332
00:17:57,290 --> 00:18:00,710
Their #4 has some serious 
height, but that's about it.

333
00:18:00,710 --> 00:18:03,260
All I remember him doing
was that crazy jump ball at the start.

334
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,130
Hm, these numbers seem very strange to me.

335
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:09,960
Perhaps he's not confident 
in his ability to shoot?

336
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:13,380
If that was true, it would make 
him a lot easier to defend.

337
00:18:13,380 --> 00:18:15,230
Should we leave him some 
room and see how it goes?

338
00:18:15,230 --> 00:18:19,170
Actually, hey Konishi, isn't this the same guy
you used to play with?

339
00:18:19,170 --> 00:18:20,380
Uh, yes.

340
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:22,710
Was he bad at scoring back in middle school?

341
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:25,430
Um, well, that...

342
00:18:26,330 --> 00:18:27,960
...that wasn't the case at all.

343
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:31,260
I honestly think that he's 
just off of his game today.

344
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,550
He just lied...

345
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:37,480
Hmm. That probably means he's been focused on

346
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:40,380
providing extra support for the last three quarters.

347
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:43,010
And I can't forget that #11 
and #15 are pretty fatigued.

348
00:18:43,290 --> 00:18:46,050
So, that means we should focus
on shoring up our defense in the middle.

349
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:49,580
With Konishi as our core player,
Tachibana and Hasebe will provide cover.

350
00:18:49,580 --> 00:18:51,130
Katori will...

351
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:57,470
The interval is over! The 
final quarter will now begin!

352
00:18:57,580 --> 00:19:00,340
Come tears or laughs, this 
is the end of it all!

353
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:02,790
Let's cap off our training 
camp with a big victory, guys!

354
00:19:02,790 --> 00:19:04,370
Yeah!

355
00:19:04,630 --> 00:19:09,720
Listen up! If you boys can't win this,
then you have no right to even try for the inter-high!

356
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:11,460
Get out there and completely crush them!

357
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:12,580
Yessir!

358
00:19:16,130 --> 00:19:18,470
I'm in love with Nao.

359
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:24,930
I'll win this game, and 
then start dating her!

360
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:29,630
Nanao is the manager for our team.
I won't let you have her.

361
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:34,300
Throw-in. Kitasumi's ball!

362
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:39,400
Okay, this is it. Let's throw 
everything we have at 'em!

363
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:42,670
Crap, it's that shorty again!

364
00:19:42,670 --> 00:19:44,920
And their zone D is even 
tighter in the middle now!

365
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:47,930
It's gotten tougher to score
from both the inside and outside!

366
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:51,710
Good grief. You really are 
just a one-trick pony!

367
00:19:51,710 --> 00:19:55,590
And let me tell you,
I know plenty of ways to deal with those!

368
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,790
Corner to corner...

369
00:19:57,790 --> 00:19:59,880
He's intentionally getting 
farther from the ball?!

370
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:03,760
They're doing an...

371
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:06,220
...overload formation!

372
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:10,010
Oh! The overload!

373
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:10,960
So, what's that?

374
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:11,830
Yeah, what?

375
00:20:11,830 --> 00:20:13,140
Let me explain...

376
00:20:13,710 --> 00:20:18,710
An overload formation focuses all of
the offensive players on one side of the court,

377
00:20:18,710 --> 00:20:21,880
which effectively pulls the members
of the defense towards them.

378
00:20:22,380 --> 00:20:28,040
With one well-placed pass,
they can easily force 2-on-1 or 3-on-2 situations,

379
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:31,080
so it's disastrous if one of 
them gets to the opposite side.

380
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:35,010
No matter what we do,
humans simply can't compete with the speed of a pass.

381
00:20:35,250 --> 00:20:38,050
Our defense has to respond 
to this carefully or else...

382
00:20:43,750 --> 00:20:45,680
Watch the other side! Adjust your positions!

383
00:20:49,710 --> 00:20:50,540
He got it!

384
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:51,800
The centers are facing off!

385
00:20:59,290 --> 00:21:01,220
Trying to get me with another fake?!

386
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,800
Defensive foul on #4! Basket 
counts! One free-throw!

387
00:21:19,830 --> 00:21:23,430
That's not enough... for 
you to beat our team.

388
00:21:25,210 --> 00:21:27,470
Dammit! Don't fuck with me!

389
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:30,630
What's up, Momoharu?

390
00:21:30,750 --> 00:21:32,340
It's nothing!

391
00:21:38,330 --> 00:21:40,960
The day that you quit playing basketball...

392
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:44,760
...do you remember what it 
is you said to me, Senpai?

393
00:21:45,250 --> 00:21:46,220
Huh?

394
00:21:48,290 --> 00:21:52,430
Back then... you lied straight to my face...

395
00:21:52,710 --> 00:21:55,260
...and I have never forgiven you for it.

396
00:23:31,010 --> 00:23:35,720
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: Higher Than Anyone

397
00:23:31,630 --> 00:23:34,550
Next episode: "Higher Than Anyone."

